  {
   "id": "note-topology",
   "type": "text",
   "position": {
    "x": 160,
    "y": 820
   },
   "data": {
    "text": "Sumo flowsheet: municipal and industrial feed meet at the primary clarifier (VKB) and pass trickling\nfilters 1+2 and 3+4 in series; the municipal overflow (everything above the switch's 3000 m\u00b3/d) and\nthe COD bypass go around them to the intermediate clarifier (ZKB), which feeds two parallel SBR\nstreets. Every SBR runs the same 7.4 h cycle, staggered against the other street.",
    "fontSize": 14
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "note-bypass",
   "type": "text",
   "position": {
    "x": 160,
    "y": 900
   },
   "data": {
    "text": "COD bypass: 250 m\u00b3/d around both filters to the ZKB, 500 m\u00b3/d while readily biodegradable COD in\nfilters 1+2 exceeds 5 mg/L. Filters ventilated by natural draft (backend default kLa).",
    "fontSize": 14
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "note-run",
   "type": "text",
   "position": {
    "x": 160,
    "y": 960
   },
   "data": {
    "text": "Run this project with a 21 day horizon: the industrial feed is a sampled weekly pulse stretched\nacross the simulated window, so a shorter run moves the pulses.",
